course: dictionary
lesson: 1914
title: Combine: join, mix, or do two things at once
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «combine» has more than one meaning. Read the words around it to find the right one, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check.
explain: To combine things is to join or mix them to make one. «Combine the flour and sugar» means put them together in the bowl.
explain: To combine can also mean to do two things at once, or to have two qualities together. «She combines school with swim training» means she does both at the same time.
explain: A combine (said COM-bine) is a big farm machine. Its full name is combine harvester, and it cuts crops like wheat.
fact: Combine means to join or mix two or more things together to make one.
fact: «Combine» can also mean to do two things at the same time, or to have two qualities together.
fact: In maths, a «combined total» is the total of two or more groups added together: 3 red counters combined with 4 blue counters make 7.
fact: A combine harvester cuts the crop, beats out the grain and blows the straw away, all at once.
fact: If you can swap in the words "join together" and the sentence still makes sense, you have the first meaning.
exercise: «Combine the flour and sugar in the bowl.» What does combine mean here? | To count slowly | To throw away | To cut into small pieces | *To mix or join together
exercise: In maths, 3 red counters and 4 blue counters combined make how many in all? | 1 | 34 | 12 | *7
exercise: «A combine harvester cuts the wheat on the farm.» What is a combine harvester? | A small toy car | A type of bread | A kind of cloud | *A big farm machine that cuts crops
test: «She combines school with swim training.» What does combines mean in this sentence? | Forgets school | Stops swimming | *Does two things at the same time | Mixes two things into one dish
test: Which phrase means the total of two groups added together? | Separate piece | Loose change | *Combined total | Half measure
exam: «To read a map well you combine three things: the directions, the scale and the legend.» What does combine mean in this sentence? | To cut the map into three | To lose the map | *To bring three things together and use them at once | To colour the map in
